  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 100 PM CDT Sun Jun 21 2026\n\nHot and humid conditions are expected through much of this coming\nwork week as the upper-level ridge continues to build across the\nregion and ample moisture remains in place across much of West\nCentral Texas through next weekend. Models are showing a stalled\nfrontal boundary draped across north Texas/southern Oklahoma \nMonday into Tuesday, keeping lower chances (20 to 30 percent) for\nshowers and a few thunderstorms across the northern portions of \nthe Big Country through early Tuesday morning. Afternoon highs\nTuesday through the end of the week could range from the mid 90s\nto as high as 106, with heat index values potentially reaching\nHeat Advisory criteria each afternoon. However, models are showing\na slightly drier trend across the area through next weekend, which\ncould help to limit the heat index values across the area. This is\nsomething we will continue to monitor closely through the week, \nas by next weekend some models are showing ambient high \ntemperatures soaring into the upper 90s along the I-10 corridor \nand well into the triple digits north of I-10.",
